[
  {
    "number": 109,
    "title": "Open qualified wall tasks in Codex Desktop",
    "body": "The wall task detail card now offers **Open in Codex** for qualified Desktop threads. The server constructs the local URI from a validated UUID: legacy tasks must appear in the current configured Desktop title index; shared tasks use their presented Codex Desktop root identity. Folded children link to their parent. CLI, Claude, unknown and malformed IDs have no link.\n\nRefs #108. Source-only; no installation or device writes.\n\nThe anchor uses native keyboard navigation and refreshes when eligibility changes. The footer and bridge guide explain that selection does not mark tasks read; opening in Codex leaves read ownership with Codex and the existing reader. Controller/integration APIs remain unchanged.\n\nValidation:\n- 460 Python tests passed, including ten new eligibility, index recovery, folded-parent, state-preservation and API-privacy cases. Missing-link regressions were observed before implementation.\n- Focused Chromium link check passed: href, no target, normal tab order, Enter activation without map action requests, eligibility changes and 390-pixel layout. The full browser suite passed with this implementation.\n- Both workflow checks passed (10 workflow tests); `git diff --check` passed.\n\nRemaining gates:\n- Windows browser-to-Codex acceptance is unverified: Computer Use fails with a non-local `sandboxCwd`; PowerShell fails with `UtilBindVsockAnyPort`, including approved escalation. A Windows-capable session/user must open one real Desktop thread from an isolated candidate map.\n- OpenSpec `gh-108-codex-thread-links` remains active with that acceptance task unchecked. Repository policy prevents synchronization/archive before acceptance evidence. Archive and final review follow that check.\n- Both independent candidate reviews found no source defects on current head `0db1b872e4cf66bb9fa8938a77dcb42de0ad65e9`. All five Depot jobs passed for that exact head and PR #109 in run `mlg7rz5695`. Explicit human approval of this UI remains required. No merge is authorized by agent review or CI alone.\n\nComparison: base/merge-base `08b6b8387268bb247e352c7e9d0604f832cad97b`, head `0db1b872e4cf66bb9fa8938a77dcb42de0ad65e9`; `git diff 08b6b8387268bb247e352c7e9d0604f832cad97b...0db1b872e4cf66bb9fa8938a77dcb42de0ad65e9`. Clean worktree at commit.\n\nExecution: coordinator implemented; one Luna/medium read-only scout identified projection and index-cache seams. Two independent Luna/high candidate reviewers used; four agent contexts total, including coordinator and scout. Both candidate review rounds are complete; round 2 covers the task-checkbox update. Runtime settings and attributable usage unknown; no advisor loop, worker corrections or promotions. Routine source work does not require a hub guide update or public publication.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/109",
